Skipped on Windows: the fat-dispatch shim selector picks register-return vs
sret from a hardcoded SysV threshold (> 16 bytes).  Win64 returns aggregates
via hidden pointer unless the size is 1/2/4/8, so this fixture's 16-byte
(Box2 int) is sret there, the selector keeps the generic forwarding shim, and
the signature mismatch jumps to a garbage address on the FIRST call.

